 # task show crashes when relationship fields are absent
 
-
+# Bug: `sandpiper-tasks task show <KEY>` crashes on certain tasks
+
+## Reproduction
+
+Observed in `~/git/pi-claude-code-cli-provider`:
+
+```bash
+cd ~/git/pi-claude-code-cli-provider
+~/.claude/skills/tasks/scripts/sandpiper-tasks task show PCCP-16
+```
+
+Output:
+
+```text
+Error: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'length')
+```
+
+The same error occurs with `--metadata-only` and with `-f json` / `-f toon`. `--no-save` does not hit the error, suggesting the crash is in render-and-save/index refresh behavior rather than basic file parsing.
+
+`task list --project PCCP` works and includes PCCP-16; other tasks such as PCCP-12 show cleanly.
+
+## Confirmed root cause
+
+`packages/sandpiper-tasks-cli/src/core/format.ts::formatTaskDetail` unconditionally reads relationship array lengths:
+
+```ts
+if (task.dependsOn.length > 0) { ... }
+if (task.blockedBy.length > 0) { ... }
+if (task.related.length > 0) { ... }
+```
+
+When frontmatter omits `depends_on`, `blocked_by`, or `related`, those properties can parse as `undefined` rather than `[]`, and `.length` throws.
+
+## Suggested fix
+
+Prefer normalizing task parser output so `dependsOn`, `blockedBy`, and `related` are always arrays after frontmatter load. Also add defensive guards in `formatTaskDetail` if useful.
+
+Add a regression test for a task with minimal frontmatter only: `title`, `status`, `kind`, `priority`, `assignee`, `reporter`, `created_at`, and `updated_at`.
+
